xtension wiring.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use the bundled "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FidoUI"},{"type":"text","text":" module for transport selection (USB-C \/ Lightning \/ NFC on iOS, HID on macOS) and for the PIN, UV, error, and success panels."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"By bypassing WebKit’s built-in WebAuthn implementation you get full control over which authenticator handles the request, the look and feel of the prompts, and access to extensions that the platform doesn’t otherwise surface.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Architecture-Overview","type":"heading","text":"Architecture Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The sample itself is intentionally thin:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Interceptor.js"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — injected into the ","type":"text"},{"code":"WKWebView","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to monkey-patch ","type":"text"},{"code":"navigator.credentials.{create,get}","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and shuttle requests\/responses through "},{"code":"WKScriptMessageHandler","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"WebView.swift"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — ","type":"text"},{"code":"UIViewRepresentable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"code":"NSViewRepresentable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" wrapper that installs the script, registers message handlers, and coordinates ceremony lifecycle (cancel on dismiss, cancel-and-replace on a new request).","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"WebAuthnHandler.swift"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — decodes the JSON envelope and calls "},{"code":"FidoUI.makeCredential","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"code":"FidoUI.getAssertion","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" with the WebView’s origin."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"ContentView.swift"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — minimal SwiftUI shell with a URL bar and back button.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"FidoUI","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" (separate Swift package under ","type":"text"},{"code":"Samples\/WebAuthnInterceptorSample\/FidoUI","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") — the reusable UI + transport layer described below."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The end-to-end flow:"}]},{"type":"orderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Page JS calls ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"navigator.credentials.create()"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".get()"},{"text":"; the interceptor serializes the options as WebAuthn Level 3 JSON and posts it to Swift.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"WebAuthnHandler"},{"type":"text","text":" decodes the JSON straight into the SDK’s strongly-typed "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Options"},{"type":"text","text":" and hands them to "},{"code":"FidoUI","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FidoUI"},{"type":"text","text":" opens a transport, runs the ceremony via "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/WebAuthn\/Client"},{"type":"text","text":", and shows PIN \/ UV \/ error \/ success panels as needed."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The resulting ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/WebAuthn\/Registration\/Response"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/WebAuthn\/Authentication\/Response"},{"type":"text","text":" is serialized via its built-in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"toJSON()"},{"type":"text","text":" and posted back to JS."}]}]}]},{"anchor":"Intercepting-WebAuthn-Calls","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Intercepting WebAuthn Calls"},{"anchor":"JavaScript-Injection","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"JavaScript Injection"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Interceptor.js"},{"type":"text","text":" replaces "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"navigator.credentials.create"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"navigator.credentials.get"},{"type":"text","text":" with versions that forward to Swift. Binary fields ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"challenge"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"user.id"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"rawId"},{"type":"text","text":", …) are serialized to "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"base64url","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" strings via "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"JSON.stringify"},{"type":"text","text":" with a replacer — this matches the WebAuthn Level 3 JSON format the SDK consumes natively, so no custom binary-wrapping protocol is needed."}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"javascript","code":["function interceptWebAuthn(type, options, originalFn) {","    if (!shouldIntercept(options)) return originalFn(options);","","    return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {","        pendingResolve = resolve;","        pendingReject = reject;","","        const publicKey = serializePublicKeyOptionsToJSON(options.publicKey);","        if (type === 'create' && publicKey.rp && !publicKey.rp.id) {","            publicKey.rp.id = window.location.hostname;","        }","","        const request = { type, request: publicKey };","        window.webkit.messageHandlers[`__webauthn_${type}__`]","            .postMessage(JSON.stringify(request));","    });","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The script is injected at document start so it runs before any page code:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["let script = WKUserScript(","    source: interceptorScript,","    injectionTime: .atDocumentStart,","    forMainFrameOnly: true",")","config.userContentController.addUserScript(script)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"shouldIntercept","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" returns ","type":"text"},{"code":"true","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for any ","type":"text"},{"code":"publicKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"-bearing request, but is the natural seam for narrower policies (e.g. only intercept when ","type":"text"},{"code":"publicKey.hints","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" includes ","type":"text"},{"code":"\"security-key\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Receiving-Messages-in-Swift","level":3,"text":"Receiving Messages in Swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Coordinator"},{"type":"text","text":" is both "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"WKNavigationDelegate"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"WKScriptMessageHandler"},{"type":"text","text":". It accepts requests from the main frame and derives their origin from WebKit. Each request starts a fresh ceremony and cancels any in-flight one first."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"shutdown()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is called from "},{"code":"dismantle{UI,NS}View","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" so navigating away mid-ceremony unwinds the open NFC\/HID handle."}]},{"level":2,"anchor":"Driving-the-Ceremony","type":"heading","text":"Driving the Ceremony"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The WebView derives the origin from the requesting main frame’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"WKSecurityOrigin"},{"text":" and passes it to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"WebAuthnHandler"},{"text":". The handler decodes the envelope and delegates to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FidoUI"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["struct WebAuthnRequest<Options: Decodable>: Decodable {","    let publicKey: Options","    enum CodingKeys: String, CodingKey { case publicKey = \"request\" }","}","","func handleCreate(_ data: Data, origin: WebAuthn.Origin) async throws -> String {","    let request = try JSONDecoder().decode(","        WebAuthnRequest<WebAuthn.Registration.Options>.self,","        from: data","    )","    let response = try await fidoUI.makeCredential(","        request.publicKey,","        origin: origin,","        serviceName: origin.host","    )","    return String(decoding: try response.toJSON(), as: UTF8.self)","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"handleGet","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is the symmetric counterpart that decodes "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/WebAuthn\/Authentication\/Options","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and calls "},{"code":"fidoUI.getAssertion","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". The response JSON produced by "},{"code":"toJSON()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is already in WebAuthn Level 3 format with base64url-encoded binary fields, so the JS side just decodes those back to "},{"code":"ArrayBuffer","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" when it materializes the credential."}]},{"text":"Returning the Response to JavaScript","level":2,"anchor":"Returning-the-Response-to-JavaScript","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The Swift-side response is JSON-encoded, base64-wrapped for the bridge, and handed back via a callback installed by the interceptor:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let encodedResponse = Data(response.utf8).base64EncodedString()","_ = try? await webView?.evaluateJavaScript(","    \"__webauthn_callback__('\\(encodedResponse)')\"",")"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"JavaScript decodes the JSON and rebuilds a "},{"code":"PublicKeyCredential","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"-shaped object — converting the base64url binary fields back to ","type":"text"},{"code":"ArrayBuffer","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"s and wiring up ","type":"text"},{"code":"getClientExtensionResults","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"getAuthenticatorData","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"getPublicKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"toJSON","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and the rest. Errors travel through a parallel ","type":"text"},{"code":"__webauthn_error__","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" channel and surface to the page as a ","type":"text"},{"code":"DOMException","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with name ","type":"text"},{"code":"NotAllowedError","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"The FidoUI Module","anchor":"The-FidoUI-Module","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"FidoUI","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is a "},{"code":"@MainActor","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" Swift package shipped alongside the sample, and it does most of the work. Intercepting "},{"code":"navigator.credentials.*","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" means giving up the platform’s built-in WebAuthn sheets (tap prompt, PIN entry, errors, success) — "},{"code":"FidoUI","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" replaces them end-to-end with a complete ceremony UI: connect \/ touch, PIN entry with retry counters, PIN change, first-time PIN setup, forced PIN-change recovery, fingerprint enrollment, credential picker, and error \/ success results. The host app stays a thin shell."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Beyond the panels, it owns the moving parts that you’d otherwise re-implement per app:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Transport selection.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" On iOS it tries wired (USB-C \/ Lightning) first and falls back to NFC. On macOS it uses HID FIDO. Connections are polled and reused across a ceremony.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Ceremony serialization."}]},{"text":" Concurrent calls on the same ","type":"text"},{"code":"FidoUI","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instance are queued so they don’t fight over the alert window, transport, or shared panel state.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Cancellation.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" A single ","type":"text"},{"code":"cancel()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" call (used by the WebView coordinator on dismiss \/ new message) tears down the active transport and dismisses any visible panel.","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Create one "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FidoUI"},{"type":"text","text":" instance per host with a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"presentationAnchor"},{"type":"text","text":" closure and an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isPublicSuffix"},{"text":" checker. Capture the initiating view weakly and return its window. The closure runs when each queued ceremony starts. If the window is unavailable, the call throws ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FidoUI.Error.presentationUnavailable"},{"text":" before opening a transport.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Call ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"makeCredential"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"getAssertion"},{"text":" for each request. The relying party must verify the returned response before completing registration or sign-in. See ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Samples\/WebAuthnInterceptorSample\/FidoUI\/"},{"text":" for the full source.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Platform Notes","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Platform-Notes"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"iOS.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" The wired path goes through CryptoTokenKit (","type":"text"},{"code":"WiredSmartCardConnection","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — USB-C or Lightning), and the NFC path through ","type":"text"},{"code":"NFCSmartCardConnection","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". The sample’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"Info.plist","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" declares ","type":"text"},{"code":"NFCReaderUsageDescription","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and lists the FIDO applet AID (","type":"text"},{"code":"A0000006472F0001","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") under ","type":"text"},{"code":"com.apple.developer.nfc.readersession.iso7816.select-identifiers","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; the entitlements turn on ","type":"text"},{"code":"com.apple.developer.nfc.readersession.formats","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"code":"TAG","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") and ","type":"text"},{"code":"com.apple.security.smartcard","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"macOS."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FidoUI"},{"text":" uses ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HIDFIDOConnection"},{"type":"text","text":". The sample enables "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"com.apple.security.device.usb"},{"type":"text","text":" for this transport."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Where to Customize","level":2,"anchor":"Where-to-Customize"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Which requests get intercepted.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" Edit "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"shouldIntercept"},{"type":"text","text":" in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Interceptor.js"},{"type":"text","text":" to scope by hint, RP ID, or any other heuristic."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Origin verification."}]},{"text":" The WebView uses the main frame’s security origin and rejects requests from child frames. Replace the ","type":"text"},{"code":"isPublicSuffix","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" closure passed to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FidoUI"},{"type":"text","text":" with a real public-suffix-list check before shipping."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"UI.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" Swap or restyle the panels in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FidoUI\/Sources\/FidoUI\/Views\/"},{"type":"text","text":" — the rest of the module is UI-agnostic."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"This sample shows how to build a FIDO2\/WebAuthn client that intercepts ","type":"text"},{"code":"navigator.credentials.{create,get}","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" calls inside a "},{"code":"WKWebView","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and routes them to a YubiKey. It uses the high-level "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/WebAuthn\/Client","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" API and delegates the entire ceremony — transport, PIN\/UV prompts, errors, cancellation — to a small ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice",